  84              - name: GIT_SHA\n  85                value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n  86            securityContext:\n  87              allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n  88              privileged: false\n  89              readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n  90              runAsNonRoot: true\n  91              capabilities:\n  92>               drop: [\"ALL\"]\n  93              seccompProfile:\n  94                type: RuntimeDefault\n  95            resources:\n  96              requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 384Mi }\n  97              limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 768Mi }\n  98            readinessProbe:\n  99              httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\n 100            volumeMounts:\n 101              - { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }\n 102              - { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }\n 103        volumes:\n 104          - name: tmp\n```\n\n## B11.2\n\n**Check:** The final image has no shell, downloader, or package manager the agent does not need.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Read the final stage of each Dockerfile (after the last `FROM`). 2) Check base image and installs for `bash`, `sh`, `curl`, `wget`, `apt`, `apk`, `pip`, `npm`. 3) Answer no if the final image has any the agent does not need, or the final stage is a full OS image (ubuntu, debian, python) not distroless or scratch.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** Dockerfile:10 — \"FROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** The final image is distroless with no shell or package manager.\n\n`Dockerfile` lines 1–22 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   1  # syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7\n   2  FROM node:22.11-bookworm-slim@sha256:3f1a8d2c9b7e4f6a5d0c8b1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a AS build\n   3  WORKDIR /app\n   4  COPY package.json package-lock.json ./\n   5  RUN npm ci --ignore-scripts\n   6  COPY tsconfig.json ./\n   7  COPY src ./src\n   8  RUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev\n   9  \n  10> FROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot@sha256:9b2e4c6a8d0f1e3c5a7b9d1f3e5c7a9b1d3f5e7c9a1b3d5f7e9c1a3b5d7f9e1c\n  11  WORKDIR /app\n  12  ENV NODE_ENV=production \\\n  13      CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT=/app\n  14  COPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/node_modules ./node_modules\n  15  COPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/dist ./dist\n  16  COPY --chown=65532:65532 package.json ./\n  17  COPY --chown=65532:65532 prompts ./prompts\n  18  COPY --chown=65532:65532 config ./config\n  19  COPY --chown=65532:65532 release ./release\n  20  USER 65532:65532\n  21  EXPOSE 8080\n  22  CMD [\"dist/server.js\"]\n```\n\n## B11.3\n\n**Check:** There is no privileged mode, hostPath or Docker socket mount, or host network or PID namespace.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Search manifests and compose for `privileged`, `hostPath`, `docker.sock`, `hostNetwork`, `hostPID`, `hostIPC`, `network_mode: host`, `pid: host`. 2) Answer no if any appears on the agent's workloads, including sidecars and init containers.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** k8s/deployment.yaml:88 — \"privileged: false\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No privileged mode, host mounts or host namespaces.\n\n`k8s/deployment.yaml` lines 76–100 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  76            image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n  77            ports:\n  78              - containerPort: 8080\n  79            envFrom:\n  80              - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n  81            env:\n  82              - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n  83                value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n  84              - name: GIT_SHA\n  85                value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n  86            securityContext:\n  87              allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n  88>             privileged: false\n  89              readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n  90              runAsNonRoot: true\n  91              capabilities:\n  92                drop: [\"ALL\"]\n  93              seccompProfile:\n  94                type: RuntimeDefault\n  95            resources:\n  96              requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 384Mi }\n  97              limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 768Mi }\n  98            readinessProbe:\n  99              httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\n 100            volumeMounts:\n```\n\n## B11.4\n\n**Check:** If the agent runs untrusted or model-written code, that code runs in a separate sandbox such as gVisor, Kata, or a microVM, not in the agent's own container.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find code execution tools (`subprocess`, `exec`, `eval`, `child_process`, `os/exec`, code interpreter). 2) Check where that code runs (`runtimeClassName: gvisor`, Kata, Firecracker, remote sandbox API). 3) Answer no if model-written or untrusted code runs in the agent's own process or container, or the sandbox call falls back to local execution on error. Answer yes if no such code runs.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** config/tools.allowlist.yaml:6 — \"- tool: ehr__find_patient\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** The agent runs no model-written code.\n\n`config/tools.allowlist.yaml` lines 1–18 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   1  # Every tool the scheduling agent may call, with the task it serves.\n   2  # The executor denies any tool not listed here. Annotations from servers (readOnlyHint and so on)\n   3  # are not used for allow or approval decisions.\n   4  role: scheduling_agent\n   5  tools:\n   6>   - tool: ehr__find_patient\n   7      reason: Match the sender to a patient record by date of birth and phone or email.\n   8    - tool: ehr__search_slots\n   9      reason: List open slots for a provider, location, and visit type.\n  10    - tool: ehr__get_appointment\n  11      reason: Read one appointment the patient asks about.\n  12    - tool: ehr__list_patient_appointments\n  13      reason: Show the patient their upcoming appointments.\n  14    - tool: ehr__book_appointment\n  15      reason: Book a slot the patient chose.\n  16    - tool: ehr__update_appointment\n  17      reason: Change time, provider, or status (confirmed / checked_in / no_show / cancelled) of an appointment.\n  18    - tool: ehr__cancel_appointment\n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to B11.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B11\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B11.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\"}],\n \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n```\nVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n","numLines":172,"startLine":1,"totalLines":172}}}
